menu "Gateway test application"

choice GATEWAY_TEST_PROFILE
    prompt "Test profile"
    default GATEWAY_TEST_PROFILE_BOARD
    help
        Which set of tests the application runs.

        The "board" profile runs every test, including the ones that need the
        real hardware (the Octal PSRAM of the N16R8, the RMT of the RGB LED,
        the radio). This is the profile that runs on the physical gateway.

        The "logic" profile skips the tests tagged [hw]. It is the profile the
        CI uses under QEMU, where the Octal PSRAM is not emulated and the
        chip would abort before the first test.

    config GATEWAY_TEST_PROFILE_BOARD
        bool "Board: every test, needs the real hardware"

    config GATEWAY_TEST_PROFILE_LOGIC
        bool "Logic: every test except the ones tagged [hw]"
endchoice

endmenu
